    "https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/p2hM7/Student-Recruitment-Coordinator-M-ori-Pasifika,2026-25237.html": {
      "title": "Student Recruitment Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Recruitment Coordinator - Māori & Pasifika -\n        Lincoln University Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search careers@lincoln.ac.nz Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Student Recruitment Coordinator - Māori & Pasifika Coordinate recruitment &engagement activities that inspire Māori and Pasifika learners to explore and pursue tertiary study opportunities. Mō te tūka | The role Join us in helping Māori and Pasifika learners discover the opportunities a tertiary education can offer. Based in our Student Engagement team, you'll coordinate and deliver recruitment and engagement initiatives that connect prospective students, whānau, schools and communities with Lincoln University. Some tasks of the role include: Coordinating school visits, campus tours, expos and community events. Building relationships with schools, whānau, iwi, hapū and community organisations. Supporting prospective students with study and programme information. Assisting with course planning and responding to enquiries. Coordinating stakeholder communications and engagement activities. Maintaining recruitment records and reporting on activities. Working closely with Te Manutaki and a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, you'll help create accessible pathways into study through culturally responsive, relationship-focused engagement. This is a rewarding opportunity to make a meaningful impact by supporting students throughout their decision-making journey and strengthening participation in tertiary education. Mahi & Wāhi / Utu | Work pattern, location & salary This fixed term role ending April 2027 is based at our Lincoln Campus and works 37.5 hours per week (1.0 FTE). The salary for this position is $57,000 - $60,000 per annum (pro-rata to fixed term), depending on experience. Kā tino Pūkeka/Whēako | Essential skills/experience for the role You will bring: Experience in customer service and relationship building. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Flexiblity to travel to events as required Confidence presenting to and engaging with different audiences. Experience working with young people from diverse backgrounds. Good organisational skills, initiative and problem-solving ability. Confidence using Microsoft 365 and working collaboratively in a team environment. Competency in te reo Māori me ōna tikaka is an advantage Alignment with Manaakitaka and Lincoln University values. Kā hua ka riro ki a koe | What's in it for you? Join a supportive, inclusive community that values diversity, wellbeing, and professional growth. Benefits include: Flexible, family‑friendly work + free on‑site parking Professional development & mentorship to grow your career Free, confidential wellbeing support through Clearhead (EAP) Southern Cross employee benefits Access to on‑campus gym with discounted membership On‑site early childhood centre with staff discounts A vibrant campus lifestyle with cafés, green spaces, and a sense of community Mō mātou | About us Te Whare Wānaka o Aoraki | Lincoln University is a specialist institution dedicated to impactful research and higher education that supports land-based industries in New Zealand and globally. Our campus sits at the heart of the Lincoln research precinct, complemented by university-owned farms and research stations that blend education, research, and hands-on learning. At Lincoln, students are at the heart of everything we do, empower them to grow their potential and contribute to a more sustainably productive world through world-class teaching and research. As a progressive university with an ambitious vision, we value a professional workforce that reflects the diversity of our community. Our staff engage with students, parents, government, iwi, and external stakeholders, upholding Lincoln University’s reputation through their work. Our Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments begin with mana whenua. We honour our special relationship with Ngāi Te Ruahikihiki and Te Taumutu Rūnanga, embedded in our He Tūtohinga Whakamātau | Charter of Understanding. Tono ināianei | Apply now Ready to apply? Submit your CV and a cover letter that highlights your fit - tell us why you want this role and what motivates you to join Lincoln University. Applications received via email will not be considered, however specific enquiry relating to the role can be made to kate.treanor@lincoln.ac.nz or bree.underhill@lincoln.ac.nz We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels valued and supported, and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. We are only considering applicants who have current unrestricted legal working rights in New Zealand. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this role. Apply now – we will review applications as they are received and may close the advertising early. View the position description at: https://careers.lincoln.ac.nz Job Details Reference # 2026-25237 Posted on 25 Aug 2026 Closes on 09 Sep 2026 18:00 NZST Location(s) Lincoln University Campus Expertise Administration, Communications, Customer Service, Marketing, Project Management, Sales Work type(s) Fixed term full-time More details (document) PD Student Recruitment Coordinator Māori Pasifika August 2026.pdf Print Email this job to a friend Apply Apply with Seek Back © Lincoln University Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 6 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
